  "_doc_look": "'look' sets per-part color (RGB, multiplied into the model texture) and scale ([length, height, width]) on top of the whole-fish 'shape'. Parts: head, bodyFront, bodyRear, tail, finDorsal, finPectoral, finBelly. Parts not listed use 'tint' and scale 1. 'whiskers' adds catfish barbels.",
  "_doc_textures": "'look.textures' patterns the model textures per role (back, belly, head, side, fin); see fishmod/tools/gen_textures.py for the operations. Patterned parts usually use a light tint.",
  "_doc_rhythm": "activity: 0-3 per time of day (dawn 4-8, day 8-17, dusk 17-20, night), from the research table in fishmod/docs/research/biomes-time-behaviour.md; 2 and up count as 'most active'. depthBand: where in the water column the fish keeps (0 = surface, 1 = floor). rise: how far up the band moves when it's active and the light is low (feeding). lightShy: how much bright light pushes it deeper. chronotypeHours: each fish's own clock is shifted by up to this many hours (carp differ by individual)."
}
